---
/**
 * The same twelve house sales, fitted twice: once by a machine with three
 * adjustable numbers and once by a machine with twelve.
 *
 * The teaching load is carried by the SHAPE of the two lines and by the two
 * scores written out underneath — a smooth rise that misses every dot slightly,
 * against a line that touches all twelve exactly and leaves the chart between
 * them. Neither panel is identified by colour, dots and squares are told apart
 * by shape as well as by tone, and both scores are stated as numbers rather
 * than implied (hard rule 9).
 *
 * Every coordinate here was sampled from the same fit the FlexibilityDial
 * instrument runs, at three dials and at twelve, so the reader meets one set of
 * sales rather than two. The quoted scores are pinned by that instrument's
 * tests, which fail if the dataset ever drifts away from these numbers.
 *
 * Decorative on its own, so `aria-hidden`: `Figure` carries the accessible name
 * and the description.
 */
